<chapter xml:id="ch-season5" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Season 5: Variables and Formulas</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> 
        Variables are letters that represent numbers that are unknown or that are changing. 
        Formulas are incomplete calculations containing variables, calculations which we can complete 
        later after the values of the variables become known. In this season, we will practice creating variables and 
        formulas that match real-world situations, and we will practice those formulas to answer real-world problems. 
      </p>
  </introduction>
